<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<main id="main">
  <div class="page-band"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Terms</p><h1>Terms of use</h1></div></div>
  <div class="page">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="muted">These terms apply to the Food Handler Certification course offered by The High Vault Security. By creating an account you agree to them. Questions: <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Register with your own legal name and a working email address. Your name is printed on your certificate.</li>
      <li>Your account is for you alone. Don’t share it or let anyone else study or sit the exam for you. Signing in on a new device signs out the previous one.</li>
      <li>Keep your password private and tell us straight away if you think someone else has used your account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The course</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The course is made up of chapters and module quizzes that unlock in order, followed by a final exam.</li>
      <li>The course teaches food safety principles. It does not replace the laws, regulations or public health requirements that apply where you work. Always follow your local public health unit.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The final exam</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You must take the exam yourself, alone, in a quiet private room, without notes, books, websites, AI tools, other people or other devices.</li>
      <li>The exam is proctored. You agree to show government-issued photo ID, record a scan of your room, and keep your camera and microphone on for the whole exam. How we handle these recordings is explained in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li>Leaving the exam page, turning off your camera or connecting another screen is recorded, and repeated warnings end the exam.</li>
      <li>Your result is final once reviewed. We may void an attempt, and revoke any certificate it produced, if the exam rules were not followed or your identity could not be confirmed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Certificates</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A certificate is issued after you pass the final exam and, where identity review applies, once the review is complete.</li>
      <li>Each certificate shows its issue and expiry dates and can be verified by anyone using its number or QR code.</li>
      <li>Whether a certificate is accepted for a particular job or inspection is decided by your employer or local public health unit. Check with them if you’re unsure.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Payments and refunds</h2>
    <p>Where the course is paid, the price is shown before you enrol and payment is processed securely by our payment provider. For refund requests, email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Don’t attempt to copy, share or sell exam questions, interfere with the platform, access other people’s accounts or data, or get around the exam’s safeguards. We may suspend accounts that do.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update the course and these terms. If we make significant changes, we’ll let registered learners know by email.</p>
  </div>
  </div>
</main>
